WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.525
Interpretation begins with observation.

00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:05.930
Describe the pattern's location, shape, size, apparent contrast, boundary,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.720
and relationship to nearby features.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.955
Avoid naming a cause before the visible evidence and operating context have been

00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:12.344
considered.

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:16.170
Compare the feature with an appropriate background or similar component under similar load

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:16.960
and conditions.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.060
A hot spot is meaningful only relative to expected behavior.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.060
Uniformly warm equipment may be normal,

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.060
while a small difference among matching components may deserve review.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.890
False impressions can come from reflections, sun loading, retained heat, airflow,

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.365
wet surfaces, insulation differences, angle, distance, or automatic display scaling.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:37.230
Moving the viewpoint or changing the comparison can help reveal a reflection without

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.280
proving the final cause.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.910
Preserve the scale and settings.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.500
Palette changes can make a small difference look dramatic.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.100
Confirm whether the file contains radiometric data and whether measurement assumptions

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.086
such as emissivity and reflected temperature are appropriate.

00:00:49.086 --> 00:00:51.440
Separate observation, judgment, and diagnosis.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.880
An observation may be an area of elevated apparent temperature.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.975
A judgment may be that it is anomalous compared with peers.

00:00:57.975 --> 00:01:02.040
A diagnosis of electrical failure or moisture intrusion requires domain evidence.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.600
Use confidence language and identify alternatives.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.405
Recommend authorized follow-up such as repeat collection, visible inspection,

00:01:08.405 --> 00:01:10.280
records review, or specialist testing.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.648
Thermal imagery is strongest when it narrows questions rather than pretending to answer

00:01:14.648 --> 00:01:14.720
every one.
